export anchor StarshipBridgeStyle:
    number: 300
    screen: CodeRepository
    name: Starship bridge
    idea: The pull request as a ship's bridge, with an arched header, a curved main viewscreen for the diff, two bevelled side consoles in orange and blue, and a check gauge that shows which system is down.
    base: dark
    palette:
        deepSpace: #060a16, the page and style sheet ground under a navy glow at the top
        console: #0e1630, console bodies, chips and rows
        consoleLight: #152044, console gradient tops and the comment
        bezel: #26355e, bezels, rims and dividers
        viewscreen: #040713, the diff screen, stations and fields
        ink: #e9eefb, text
        steel: #a3b2d3, labels and meta
        bridgeOrange: #ff9f45, headings, the current tab, the primary button, changes requested and the arch rule
        signalBlue: #62b3ff, data, passed, approved, added lines, the open state and focus
        alert: #ff7d88, the failing system and removed lines
        alertShade: #2c1324, the failing row and removed line ground
    type:
        A rounded geometric sans, Avenir Next, Segoe UI, Ubuntu, Trebuchet
        MS, for text at 15px and 1.5. Its condensed cut, Avenir Next
        Condensed, Segoe UI Semibold, Ubuntu Condensed, at 600 for the
        title and repository at 30 to 32px and console titles at 13px caps
        tracked 0.18em in orange. Labels are 11px caps tracked 0.18em, the
        diff 13px monospace.
    layout:
        The header is an arch, a dark navy band whose bottom edge curves
        down in a wide ellipse with a 2px orange rule. It holds a round B
        badge and the app name, pill counters on the right, the repository
        centred with an orange Private pill, and a centred row of pill tabs
        with the current one filled orange. The body has three columns,
        280px, flexible and 280px. The left console sweeps its top right
        corner in an 80px curve and holds Systems, a half ring gauge of
        twelve segments, blue for passed and a dashed red segment with a
        cross for e2e-android, the caption 11 of 12, the failing line and
        all checks in two columns. The centre viewscreen has an elliptical
        top edge, an inner rim and a faint blue glow, with the Open pill,
        the title and number and the merge sentence centred above the file
        bar and the diff. The comment is an orange rimmed Hail bubble. The
        right console mirrors the curve and holds Crew, two rounded reviewer
        cards with ringed initials, then assignee, labels, milestone,
        linked issue and a dashed disabled merge button. A Helm strip runs
        across the bottom with a curved lower edge and three file stations.
        Below 1100px the viewscreen leads, below 700px all stack.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 20px between consoles, 20px console padding, 28px under the arch.
    density: Medium. A centred viewscreen flanked by two consoles and a helm strip below.
    corners: Curved. Elliptical arch, viewscreen and helm edges, consoles with one sweeping 80px corner, pill tabs and buttons, 14px stations.
    borders: 2px navy bezel rims, a 2px orange rule under the arch and around the comment.
    shadows: Deep drop shadows under consoles, inset rims and a faint blue glow inside the viewscreen.
    icons:
        1.9px rounded line icons. A tick for passed, an octagon cross for
        failing, a ringed tick for approved, a triangle for changes, and
        gauge segments with a cross for the failing check.
    focus: A 3px signal blue outline offset 3px.
    tone: Calm bridge words, such as Systems, Crew, Helm, Station, Hail and Standing by until all checks pass.
